<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH IPB 1996 NET PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>CZECH IPB 1996 NET PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>After-tax 1996 profit of Czech bank Investicni a Postovni Banka a.s., according to international accounting standards (IAS), rose to 1.51 billion crowns from 1.01 billion crowns in 1995, according to filings with the Prague Stock Exchange (PSE) obtained on Monday.  </p>
<p> pre-tax profit (czk million)  1,559.700   vs  1,372.000</p>
<p> taxation				(49.845)  vs   (365.000)</p>
<p> after-tax profit		  1,509.855   vs  1,007.000</p>
<p> pre-tax profit (czk million)  1,559.700   vs  1,372.000</p>
<p> total assets		    234,700.939  vs 197,271.000</p>
<p> basic capital		     5,681.497  vs   3,731.000</p>
<p>Note. Further results were not yet available, and all</p>
<p>results are subject to an external audit. The bank has called</p>
<p>its regular annual general meeting to be held on June 26.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
